# Originality and stump design

Design the failure mode first. The model should miss because a real applicability condition is easy to drop, not because the English is foggy.

Allowed pressure: activity vs concentration, wrong $n$, illegal small-$x$, identical-particle sign, stated non-default standard state, which operator is measured, reading-frame after a stated splice, neglected junction.

Forbidden: ambiguous referents, hidden definitions, riddles, MC/T-F, contest clones with integers swapped, paraphrases of `docs/examples/gold-harned-cell/`, or the previous draft in `submissions/`.

If the last problem opened with a cell diagram, the next one must not. Rotate the scientific object: rate law, Hamiltonian, pedigree, sequence plus a code table, circuit with element values, enzyme numbers.

PDF example problems (pages 75–96) are scientific inspiration only. The PDF says they are not the project's LaTeX standard.

If both hard models solve it, change the science. Do not thicken the wording.
